\def\@LN@column{1}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The price list, verified on trained checkpoints. Left: the retention half-life $n_{1/2}$ against the analytic tilt $\delta $ that sets the transverse curvature. The overdamped branch follows the predicted law at fitted slope $-0.985$ against a predicted $-1$ and then saturates, past the crossover $h=h^*(\gamma )$, at the curvature-independent floor $27.03$ steps at $\gamma =0.05$; the two retention metrics --- envelope half-life (circles) and raw first-crossing time (squares) --- agree through the overdamped band and separate underdamped, by up to $3.2\times $ at the deepest tilt, which is the exceptional point's second-order signature and the reason every lifetime in this paper names its metric. Right: the underlying curvature identity, measured over predicted spectral mass, flat at $1.000000\pm 5\times 10^{-12}$ across $4.5$ decades of $\delta $. \emph  {Trained designed checkpoints carrying analytic tilts, $5$ seeds, dim $4$, $\gamma =0.05$, laptop CPU: verification of the theory's exactness. The full battery, the probe's own roundoff floor and the damping corollary are in Appendix~\ref {app:gmor}.}}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pricelist}{{1}{5}{The price list, verified on trained checkpoints. Left: the retention half-life $n_{1/2}$ against the analytic tilt $\delta $ that sets the transverse curvature. The overdamped branch follows the predicted law at fitted slope $-0.985$ against a predicted $-1$ and then saturates, past the crossover $h=h^*(\gamma )$, at the curvature-independent floor $27.03$ steps at $\gamma =0.05$; the two retention metrics --- envelope half-life (circles) and raw first-crossing time (squares) --- agree through the overdamped band and separate underdamped, by up to $3.2\times $ at the deepest tilt, which is the exceptional point's second-order signature and the reason every lifetime in this paper names its metric. Right: the underlying curvature identity, measured over predicted spectral mass, flat at $1.000000\pm 5\times 10^{-12}$ across $4.5$ decades of $\delta $. \emph {Trained designed checkpoints carrying analytic tilts, $5$ seeds, dim $4$, $\gamma =0.05$, laptop CPU: verification of the theory's exactness. The full battery, the probe's own roundoff floor and the damping corollary are in Appendix~\ref {app:gmor}.}}{figure.1}{}}
