\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The headline laws of the price list survive the shipped anchor cure at $3000$ epochs ($\approx 20\times $ the erosion horizon; anchored $\lambda {=}100$, $3$ seeds). Left: the retention law $n_{1/2}$ versus tilt $\delta $ --- anchored-$3000$-epoch points on the predicted slope, fitted $-0.961$ against predicted $-1$, saturating at the curvature-independent floor $27.03$; the $\mu ^2/\delta $ ratio is $1.0000\pm 10^{-12}$ over $4.6$ decades. Right: the exceptional-point onset $\varphi \propto \sqrt  {h-h^*}$ above the exceptional point, fitted slope $0.516$ against predicted $0.5$, with $\varphi =0$ exactly below --- bit-identical to the $150$-epoch value. \emph  {Designed testbed under the shipped cure; the survival of the laws through $3000$ erosive epochs is evidence for the recipe.}}}{10}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sf3}{{3}{10}{The headline laws of the price list survive the shipped anchor cure at $3000$ epochs ($\approx 20\times $ the erosion horizon; anchored $\lambda {=}100$, $3$ seeds). Left: the retention law $n_{1/2}$ versus tilt $\delta $ --- anchored-$3000$-epoch points on the predicted slope, fitted $-0.961$ against predicted $-1$, saturating at the curvature-independent floor $27.03$; the $\mu ^2/\delta $ ratio is $1.0000\pm 10^{-12}$ over $4.6$ decades. Right: the exceptional-point onset $\varphi \propto \sqrt {h-h^*}$ above the exceptional point, fitted slope $0.516$ against predicted $0.5$, with $\varphi =0$ exactly below --- bit-identical to the $150$-epoch value. \emph {Designed testbed under the shipped cure; the survival of the laws through $3000$ erosive epochs is evidence for the recipe.}}{figure.3}{}}
