\def\@LN@column{1}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Autonomous retention on the $S^1$ protocol of the equivariant-Lyapunov preprint (arXiv:2605.03338): a phase is written, the input is removed, and the drift of the stored phase is tracked across recurrent-map applications. The learned baselines lose the stored phase within $\approx 5.6/56/69$ map-steps (coRNN/LEM/LSTM) and the stored coordinate randomizes past $1.2$ rad; the generically-trained unit holds a bounded $\approx 0.35$ rad and the symmetry-designed unit does not move. \emph  {Multi-seed status, stated plainly:} each baseline curve is the median over $5$ seeds and the emergent curve the median over $3$ seeds, while the designed curve is a single representative checkpoint --- the $5/5$-seed latch statement is \S  \ref {sec:boundary}'s, not this figure's. Dim $4$, hidden $64$, laptop CPU, drift threshold $0.2$ rad, $T=0$. \emph  {Evidence.}}}{12}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:retention}{{4}{12}{Autonomous retention on the $S^1$ protocol of the equivariant-Lyapunov preprint (arXiv:2605.03338): a phase is written, the input is removed, and the drift of the stored phase is tracked across recurrent-map applications. The learned baselines lose the stored phase within $\approx 5.6/56/69$ map-steps (coRNN/LEM/LSTM) and the stored coordinate randomizes past $1.2$ rad; the generically-trained unit holds a bounded $\approx 0.35$ rad and the symmetry-designed unit does not move. \emph {Multi-seed status, stated plainly:} each baseline curve is the median over $5$ seeds and the emergent curve the median over $3$ seeds, while the designed curve is a single representative checkpoint --- the $5/5$-seed latch statement is \S \ref {sec:boundary}'s, not this figure's. Dim $4$, hidden $64$, laptop CPU, drift threshold $0.2$ rad, $T=0$. \emph {Evidence.}}{figure.4}{}}
